# slate-sudoers — amendment requested 2026-06-29
#
# This file is the proposed diff to /etc/sudoers.d/020_slate to give
# Slate NOPASSWD access to manage timesheet-web.service. Permission asked
# for explicitly by Jack in chat 2026-06-29 19:21, after repeated
# "orphaned-nohup" incidents where I had to fall back to starting the
# Flask app outside systemd because I couldn't `systemctl restart`.
#
# To apply:
#   sudo -e /etc/sudoers.d/020_slate
# (opens the live file in your editor)
#
# In the editor:
#   1. Append the new alias block below.
#   2. Add SLATE_TIMESHEET to the comma-separated NOPASSWD list at the
#      bottom of the file (so it sits next to SLATE_PKG, SLATE_SVC, ...).
#   3. Save and exit. sudo runs visudo -c on it before installing.
#
# What this grants (and does NOT grant):
#   - systemd verbs for ONE unit: timesheet-web.service
#   - daemon-reload, so I can apply a unit-file edit without you
#   - read-side is-active/is-failed/status/show
#   - edit verbs: NONE (I won't `edit`, `cat`, or `tee` a unit file
#     from this scope — those would be a different grant)
#   - verbs that touch other services: NONE
#   - verbs that bypass the unit boundary (`systemctl --no-ask-password`,
#     `systemctl kill`, `systemctl mask`, `systemctl set-property`):
#     NONE
#
# Why I want this and not just bash the timesheet harder:
#   - I'm not the only thing managing that port; when systemd is in a
#     failed state because of a start-restart-too-quickly loop,
#     `systemctl reset-failed` is the only safe way out, and I need sudo
#     for that
#   - The "bounce for a code edit" path is currently `kill -TERM PID &&
#     nohup app.py &` which created an orphan this session at 18:58;
#     that's a memory leak (in the operational sense) of the same bug
#     twice in one day
#   - Kill switch is the existing `slate-revoke.sh` -- removing this
#     file leaves everything else intact

# --- Service management: only timesheet-web.service, only the verbs
#     we actually need (incl. daemon-reload for unit-file changes
#     Jack applies; granted 2026-06-29) ---
Cmnd_Alias SLATE_TIMESHEET = /usr/bin/systemctl restart timesheet-web.service, \
                             /usr/bin/systemctl start timesheet-web.service, \
                             /usr/bin/systemctl stop timesheet-web.service, \
                             /usr/bin/systemctl status timesheet-web.service, \
                             /usr/bin/systemctl is-active timesheet-web.service, \
                             /usr/bin/systemctl is-failed timesheet-web.service, \
                             /usr/bin/systemctl reset-failed timesheet-web.service, \
                             /usr/bin/systemctl show timesheet-web.service, \
                             /usr/bin/systemctl daemon-reload

# Apply this by changing the existing bottom-of-file line from:
#   pi ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: SLATE_PKG, SLATE_SVC, SLATE_CONF, SLATE_USR, SLATE_FW
# to:
#   pi ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: SLATE_PKG, SLATE_SVC, SLATE_CONF, SLATE_USR, SLATE_FW, SLATE_TIMESHEET

# Test it (you):
#   sudo -n systemctl is-active timesheet-web.service   # 0 or 3, no password
#   sudo -n systemctl daemon-reload                       # 0, no password
